        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(control-ui): show unavailable sizes for negative byte counts",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nFixes an issue where Control UI status details could render an invalid negative byte count as a normal byte-size value, such as `-1 B`, instead of showing the existing unavailable marker.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\n`formatBytes()` is the Control UI wrapper that decides when byte-size data is displayable. Missing and non-finite values already render as `-`; this change treats negative byte counts the same way because byte counts are cardinal values and a negative count is not a meaningful UI size.\n\nThe shared `formatByteSize()` helper remains unchanged. It still formats caller-provided numbers with the requested unit style; the Control UI wrapper now rejects this invalid display input before delegating to that shared formatter. Existing zero and positive formatting remains unchanged.\n\n## User Impact\n\nUsers now see `-` for malformed or sentinel-like negative byte metrics instead of a misleading negative size label. Normal Control UI byte displays such as `0 B`, `512 B`, and `1.5 KB` are preserved.\n\n## Evidence\n\nAfter-fix terminal proof from the current branch source. The temporary local script reads `ui/src/lib/agents/display.ts`, evaluates the exported `formatBytes()` function body, and imports the real shared formatter from `packages/normalization-core/src/format.ts`:\n\n```text\nControl UI byte formatter after-fix proof (current branch source)\nformatBytes source: ui/src/lib/agents/display.ts\nformatByteSize source: packages/normalization-core/src/format.ts\nguard line: if (bytes == null || !Number.isFinite(bytes) || bytes < 0) {\nformatBytes(-1): -\nformatBytes(0): 0 B\nformatBytes(512): 512 B\nformatBytes(1536): 1.5 KB```\n\nFocused regression coverage added:\n- `formatBytes(-1)` returns `-`\n- existing zero and positive byte formatting assertions remain unchanged\n\nValidation:\n- `git diff --check` passed\n- `pnpm --dir ui test -- src/lib/agents/display.test.ts` was attempted locally, but the command ran the full UI suite and hit local environment failures unrelated to this diff: Chinese locale-formatted strings, missing Playwright Chromium, and a pre-existing Vite alias assertion. No production files outside `ui/src/lib/agents/display.ts` and `ui/src/lib/agents/display.test.ts` were changed.\n\nAI-assisted: drafted and validated with Codex; I reviewed the change and understand the behavior.",
